/*
We have N machines. Using machine i once consumes A[i] calories and costs 1 ticket.
Atsushi has M tickets.

Rule:
For every i (1 <= i < N), the number of times machine i can be used is at most
the number of times machine i+1 is used.
So if x[i] is usage count of machine i, then:
x1 <= x2 <= ... <= xN
and sum x[i] <= M, x[i] >= 0 integers.

We need maximize sum A[i] * x[i].

Key transformation:
Let y[k] be how many times all machines k..N are increased together.
Then:
x[i] = y[1] + y[2] + ... + y[i]
equivalently, if we define z[k] as number of layers starting at machine k,
then total tickets used by one layer starting at k is (N-k+1),
and gained calories are prefix/suffix sum of A over k..N.

More directly:
Any feasible nondecreasing x can be decomposed into choosing some number of
"suffix bundles":
bundle k uses one ticket on each machine k..N
cost = N-k+1 tickets
value = sum_{i=k..N} A[i]

Since bundles can be taken unlimited times, this becomes an unbounded knapsack:
maximize value with total cost <= M.

Let:
cost len = len (suffix length)
value[len] = sum of last len machines

Then dp[t] = max calories with exactly/at most t tickets.
Unbounded knapsack:
dp[t] = max(dp[t], dp[t-len] + value[len]) for all len<=t

Answer = max dp[0..M], but since all values are nonnegative in this setting usually
using more tickets is never worse; still we compute dp[M] with standard max formulation.

Complexity: O(N*M)

This matches typical constraints when intended for DP.
*/

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        FastScanner fs = new FastScanner(System.in);

        int N = fs.nextInt();
        int M = fs.nextInt();

        long[] a = new long[N + 1];
        for (int i = 1; i <= N; i++) a[i] = fs.nextLong();

        long[] suffix = new long[N + 2];
        for (int i = N; i >= 1; i--) suffix[i] = suffix[i + 1] + a[i];

        // value[len] = calories of using the last len machines once each
        long[] value = new long[N + 1];
        for (int len = 1; len <= N; len++) {
            value[len] = suffix[N - len + 1];
        }

        long[] dp = new long[M + 1];
        for (int t = 1; t <= M; t++) {
            long best = dp[t];
            for (int len = 1; len <= N && len <= t; len++) {
                best = Math.max(best, dp[t - len] + value[len]);
            }
            dp[t] = best;
        }

        System.out.println(dp[M]);
    }

    static class FastScanner {
        private final InputStream in;
        private final byte[] buffer = new byte[1 << 16];
        private int ptr = 0, len = 0;

        FastScanner(InputStream is) {
            in = is;
        }

        private int read() throws IOException {
            if (ptr >= len) {
                len = in.read(buffer);
                ptr = 0;
                if (len <= 0) return -1;
            }
            return buffer[ptr++];
        }

        long nextLong() throws IOException {
            int c;
            do {
                c = read();
            } while (c <= ' ' && c != -1);

            int sign = 1;
            if (c == '-') {
                sign = -1;
                c = read();
            }

            long val = 0;
            while (c > ' ') {
                val = val * 10 + (c - '0');
                c = read();
            }
            return val * sign;
        }

        int nextInt() throws IOException {
            return (int) nextLong();
        }
    }
}
